There are a few other things to consider "if matlab is not an issue"--one of
which is the performance of the compiled language applications you would
like to run. Using Tru64 & the Compaq C/C++ & Fortran compilers will provide
you with a 5-50% performance improvement over using the Linux/gcc
combination, depending on your exact application. Using the Compaq compilers
for Alpha Linux (free for "enthusiasts") will reduce this difference, but
certainly not erase it as Tru64 is (naturally) highly optimized for the AXP
platform, whereas Linux runs on everything from 386's to S/390's. If
performance is critical, you might enroll for the Compaq smartdrive program
where you can get access to some really big kahuna Compaq hardware for 30
days or so to try it out. They have systems running Tru64 & various flavors
of Linux.

HTH,
matt.

