Pixel (pixelised@hotmail(DOT)com) wrote:

: Well I am using the text version of the installer... that's where I am
: getting the exception occurred message straight after everything is
: installed...

If you have troubles after "everything" (actually "enough" will work as
well but requires more fiddling) is installed then do not worry too
much.  Reboot from your installation media but do not request your
ramdisk and give "root=<a partition with your newly created file
system>".  For example something like that, using SRM and a floppy,

  b dva0 -fi vmlinux.gz -fl "root=/dev/sda1"

or even

  b dva0 -fi vmlinux.gz -fl "root=/dev/sda1 single"

if things are in a pretty bad shape.  Similar if you boot via milo.
Your system should boot and you can finish a cleanup (proper
/etc/fstab, booting, network configuration, ....) from there.
Your distribution CD is fit for booting as well.

Remember, if you managed to _start_ an installation then you were
already running Linux.

  Michal




