Well I have had one running with Redhat 5.2 which was recently
upgraded to Debian 2.2. I'm quite sure you are going to have problems
if you have a tape drive connected to the Qlogic controller and use
kernel 2.2.1x - this makes it lock... You can try and take out the tape
drive out and compile an older kernel. I'm using kernel 2.2.4 which
works fine.
Regarding the Mylex controller. If your firmware is older than 3.5x
your out of luck. If you have the guts for it you could try FreeBSD
which supports DAC960 using all firmware versions.

