of
>> them use 2048 Bytes, however, and not all of them can be switched to
>> 512.

M> I only booted off a winnt cd to install winnt.

I'm not sure, but it's nonetheless possible that the block size is 2048
bytes; the ARC console behaves differently (example: the HALT switch
doesn't work in ARC), so I don't know whether this block size issue is
an SRM only restriction.

It is essential on the Jensen that NT and Linux reside on different
disks (not just on two partitions, but physical disks). This is a
requirement if you want to install both operating systems, because NT
wants a PC style partition table and SRM a BSD disklabel on the boot
disk. This is no excuse, however, for not booting off the CD-ROM.

M>>> I am looking on the web now for documentation on this error, and
will
