machine
>> that is known to be able to boot from CD, if you have one available.

Well, to the best of my knowledge, the most probable reasons are:
1)  The CD isn't bootable
2)  SRM can't boot off the CD-ROM drive

M> To start JumpStart! normally on a Jensen system, follow the
instructions
M> listed in part a. for determining the SRM device name of the CD-ROM
drive
M> and then type:
M> >>> boot [the device name] -fl 3

Well, you already seem to know all the important things: this is
correct and should work; possibly interfering environment settings
(BOOTDEV_DEF and BOOT_OSFLAGS, IIRC) are overridden.

Regards, Christoph



