You can add more stanzas like the above to that file with any
labels you want.  There is actually another possible line which
looks like this:
         append="here a string of extra kernel options"

: Is there an option I can add in milo.conf  I can use to boot linux as
: default?

Unfortunately none of milos around, AFAIK, implements 'timeout='
directive if you are thinking about autoboot.  Use OSLOADOPTIONS in
ARC (or derivatives) menus for that and set timeout there.  Results
will be pretty close.

: Can I add an extra boot configuration?

Why you will not simply try?  Nothing bad may happen as you can
still boot directly from a MILO> prompt.

I have usually a few kernels around and corresponding stanzas in
milo.conf.  Saves a lot on typing (and mistyping :-).

For those with SRM /etc/aboot.conf gives similar capabilities
but there you are limited to "only" 10 boot lines labelled by
single decimal digits.

: Please direct me to the right documentation.

You have all to what is to know above.

