  I thought this might be of interest to some in this newsgroup, 
since you were tossing around sizeof-reporting code:

  http://www.andansbutt.org/ttk/stdtypes/stdtypes101.tar

  It's an application that runs on your host system and generates
an "stdtypes.h" file that defines a bunch of known-sized types 
and other potentially useful system-dependent information.  I use
it quite a lot to generate platform-independent code more easily.

  Adding it to an application distribution can be as easy as 
adding "stdtypes.h" to its Makefile's "all" rule, and then adding
a rule:

stdtypes.h: stdtypes.c
	$(CC) -o stdtypes stdtypes.c $(LIB)
	./stdtypes

(add whatever trimming your Makefile needs, of course)

