On the last page, it says
-----------------------------------------
1.  Mount the Alpha Firmware CD on a PC and copy the appropriate
    file, as shown in the table below, onto a blank, FAT-formatted
    diskette.

    System           Firmware CD Directory   File Name

    AlphaPC 164LX       ALPHAPC164LX         LX164SRM.ROM
    AlphaPC 164SX       ALPHAPC164SX         SX164SRM.ROM

    IMPORTANT: The file must not be renamed to something other
    than the file name shown above, and the file must be placed
    in the top-most (root) directory on the floppy diskette, or
    the file will not be found by the AlphaBIOS firmware update
    utility.

2.  Place the floppy in the target system, and from the AlphaBIOS
    setup menu, select "AlphaBIOS Update".
-------------------------------------------------
The file size of LX164SRM.ROM is 542K.

B. On
http://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/readmes/alphapc164lx.html#method_AlphaBIOS,

--------------------------------------------------------
AlphaBIOS Update Floppy

    1.From the table below, download the appropriate firmware update
image(s) from
      the alphapc164lx directory in the V5.8 CD area

       Firmware Image
       lx164_v5_8.exe


    2.Copy the downloaded file(s) to a blank FAT formatted floppy as :

      fwupdate.exe

      IMPORTANT: The filename must remain what you downloaded it as, and
must be
      placed in the top-most level (root) directory on the floppy, or
the image file
      will not be found properly.

    3.Place the floppy in the target system, and from the AlphaBIOS
menu, select
      "Update AlphaBIOS".
--------------------------------------------------
The file lx164_v5_8.exe is 1140k.

C. There is another lx164srm.rom (of size 456k) in
http://www.alpha-processor.com/products/downloads/customer_support/LX/

Among those A, B, and C, I chose A.  and failed miserably.
