mw wrote:
> 
> Hi
> I've got AlphaPC164lx and UPS connected via RS232.
> UPS shuts off when the RTS line is activated.Unfortunately, immadiately
> after switching my comp. on, the UPS is switching off! By this way the
> system can fall into the loop: UPS turns on comp. and comp. turns off
> UPS!
> I think it's caused by POST procedure which tests the UART.
> Is it able to turn off testing of the UART? And how to do it from SRM
> concole?
> (with common PC komputer UPS works properly)
> MW
> 
> 

You didn't mention what type of UPS you're using but typically UPS
serial ports require a cable that connect only SD, RD and SIGGND --
you use them with no hardware handshaking.  As you've noticed, when
you ground RTS pins some UPSs will turn off.  That's so you can wire a
switch for that purpose.  

So, wire up a cable with only those three connections and connect that
between your computer and UPS.

Barry



