You have to add the partition number where the linux root image is...

MILO> boot hda4:/kernels/generic.gz root=/dev/hda4
In the above example milo will look in partition 4 for the
/kernels/generic.gz   BUT if you installed linux the kernel is actually in
/boot   /kernel/generic.gz is to boot the CD from SRM

You could use fdisk to find your linux native partition is you do not
remember where it was installed.

