Hi Kumaran,

I kind of boot the same way. However, you should include the partition that
you want to load kernel of and the partition you want to mount as root.

I'm not sure if you have a SCSI drive (sda) or and IDE drive (hda)?

My SCSI disk has 7 partitions (sda7 is the /boot partition and sda5 is /) and
I boot the following way:

MILO> boot sda7:vmlinuz root=/dev/sda5

If you have only one partition, it is often sda2 or hda2. You can also do a
"help", "show" and "ls hda*:" (try 1-9 for the *).

Good luck!

Cheers,

Olger
olger.stoelinga@cmg.nl


