Michael wrote:
> Has anyone used the Compaq alpha jumpstart cd (with any success)?

yeah, we used it last night to install RH6.2 onto an es40 using only
the serial console. Worked well. It's a really nice install and
recovery tool.
The jumpstart kernel is also pretty nice (2.2.16 + BIGMEM + ???) as
we can see all 8G of memory.

The problems we had with jumpstart are that it forgot to tell us to
put "console=ttyS0", and maybe "-text"(*) at the end of the RedHat
install boot command, but this only applies to headless installs.
The Jumpstart kernel is also pretty minimal and didn't come with
(for example) the kernel modules for eepro100 (to drive the network
card that Compaq shipped us) and autofs. I don't see why the
Jumpstart people just don't compile up a fairly complete set of
modules and kernel options by default... However as the kernel
sources are on the Jumpstart CD we could compile these modules 
ourselves and drop them into the running kernel with no unforseen
hassles.

Our main problem was that the RedHat text-only installer crashed
right at the end (not Jumpstart's problem), and Jumpstart made
recovering the system after this RedHat stuffup MUCH simpler.

