At the SRM prompt type

set os_type VMS   to change to vms console, or
set os_type unix    to unix

then type "init"

You should not have to change it from unix though.  The problem most likely
is  the console firmware does not recognize your CD as one it supports.  try
booting from floppies.

if you have a windows system put the CD in and goto the images directory,
there are disk (floppy) images there you can copy to floppies (using
rawrite) to perform the install.  Once the linux kernel starts it will be
able to talk with the CD through its drivers.  the rawrite utility is also
on the cd, if not under images, then look in "tools".

boot image and ramdisk image are whats needed.

command  "boot dqa0 -fi vmlinux.gz  -fl "root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1 "

be sure to check the "use fdisk" button on the Installation type display.
and use "BSD style labels or you will not be able to boot.

JJ

