I'm not familiar with Alphaserver 2000, but I assume it uses the SRM console.
You can find out about SRM at http://www.alphalinux.org.  Follow the link to SRM
Howto or AlphaBIOS Howto.
Even so, there's some stuff it won't tell you very easy.

Typically, to boot a linux rescue floppy, use a boot command like this:
boot dva0 -file vmlinuz -flags "root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1"
which can be abbreviated
b dva -fi vmlinuz -fl "root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1"
Other suggestions for boot files:  vmlinux, linux, linux.gz, vmlinux.gz
If all else fails, suppose you get to the aboot> prompt, you can do a dir of the
drive and see the file name.

