Not my url :^)   I had not been there in a while, he has removed some info.
The bottom line is, if you have a DAC960 from Digital. (kzpac i believe)  it
contains only one firmware chip and the code and is based of V2 firmware
from mylex. Linux WILL NOT run this board.  It was possible to upgrade some
of the later (last-year) boards that had both firmware chip sockets
installed so the firmware could be upgraded to the V3 base from mylex
(needs two roms).

Aside from all that. you would need the RCU (Raid Configuration Utility) to
configure the raid sets. I'll assume you got one with the box..   install
the floppy and type RCU  it should start the arc/alphabios console and run
the RCU from floppy.  You can then configure your physical and logical
drives into various raid sets.


Your error
 waiting for dra.0.0.7.0 to poll".

means it sees a drive but does not see response to an init.  It will sit
there till the firmware times out..
.ie. put the jumper back to its original place.

JJ

